# vergeio_tenant_copy (Resource)

Copies a tenant's current state and keeps the copy in state. Destroy deletes the copy. The source tenant is only read.

This is not a snapshot clone. The pinned govergeos client clones a tenant with `Tenants.Clone`. That call takes `name`, `no_vnet`, `no_storage`, and `no_nodes`. It has no snapshot argument. `tenant_actions` `restore` sends `params.snapshot` and overwrites the source tenant. This resource does not call it. A copy from a system snapshot needs `cloud_snapshot_tenant_actions` action `recover`. The pinned client does not expose that call.

`isolate` defaults to true and posts `isolateon` on the copy when it is not already isolated. This resource does not post `isolateoff`. Set `isolate` to false to keep the connectivity the clone copied.

This is not the [`vergeio_tenant_clone` action](../actions/tenant_clone.html). That action copies a tenant and does not keep the copy in state.

An apply that is interrupted after VergeOS stores the copy keeps that key in state and returns the error. The next apply destroys the copy instead of failing because the name already exists. `created` is the time VergeOS stored the copy. Refresh drops this resource when the key's name or `created` time differs. Destroy without a refresh leaves that other tenant.

