## Schema

### Required

- `name` (String) Name of the copy. Changing it replaces the copy.
- `tenant_id` (String) Source tenant key, the same value as `vergeio_tenant.id`. Changing it replaces the copy. This tenant is not modified.

### Optional

- `isolate` (Boolean) Post `isolateon` on the copy when it is not already isolated. Defaults to true. false leaves the connectivity the clone copied, including isolation copied from the source. This resource does not post `isolateoff`. Refresh keeps this value.

### Read-Only

- `created` (Number) Unix time when VergeOS created the copy. Distinct from `id`, which VergeOS can reuse. A different name or created time means the key now points at another tenant, and refresh drops this resource. Destroy without a refresh leaves the other tenant. Import leaves this empty, and the first read stores it.
- `id` (String) Tenant key of the copy.

## Import

Import with the copy's tenant key, or `source/copy` when the source tenant key is known. A copy key alone is enough for refresh. `source/copy` also stores `tenant_id`. Import stores `isolate` as true, the default. Refresh keeps that value. It does not copy the tenant `isolate` field, because `false` leaves copied connectivity in place and does not post `isolateoff`.

```shell
terraform import vergeio_tenant_copy.example 40
terraform import vergeio_tenant_copy.example 7/40
```
